@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Inputs}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_NumericInput}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview_Tests}")]

@inject ILiveRegionService _liveRegionService

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Numeric_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Numeric_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</h1>

    <p>
        The Numeric Input component in this library is the combination of a label, optional hint area, an input that can have its <span class="code-span">inputmode</span> attribute set to <b>numeric or decimal</b> (for whole or fractional numbers respectively), and a region below the input for
        validation messages.
    </p>

</section>


<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        The examples below only use two fields, <b>Units In Stock</b> and <b>Unit Price</b>, each of which is marked as required along with having validation rules. The "Units In Stock" field/input is
        of type integer whilst the "Unit Price" field is of type decimal with a format string for currency. "Units In Stock" requires a value between 1 and 999 (inclusive) and "Unit Price" requires a price
        between 1 and 99999 (inclusive).
    </p>
    <p>
        For the examples the following Validation Display options are used in each test so you can test the options with your chosen devices.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Described By With Hint -  This options links the input to the hint text via the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute. The id of unordered list element that holds any validation errors
            is added or removed from the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute, depending on the validity of the value. The id of the validation errors element is places first in the attribute.
        </li>
        <li>
            Described By Hint Suppressed - This option removes the id of the hint text element from the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute when there are validation errors to reduce verbosity
            for screen reader users.
        </li>
        <li>
            Tabbable With Hint - This option only uses the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute for the hint text element which is never removed. The Validation errors area is given a tab stop
            and is promoted to a landmark regions. In the following examples these transient regions will have the accessible name of [Label Text] + " errors" so for a "Unit Price" field the region would be "Unit Price errors".
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        For each of the above options there are two examples, one that uses Blazors <span class="code-span">oninput</span> event which causes validation on every keystroke the other using the <span class="code-span">onchange</span> event
        which occurs if the value has changed and once focus is lost.
    </p>
    <p>
        Examples one to three use the "On Input" event whilst examples four to six use the "On Change" event.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Important: </strong>Some screen reader and browser combinations treat the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute similar to a live regions so when the hint text id or errors element id is added/removed
        with validation screen reader users will get announcements which may be distracting. This behaviour may differ with the event used, for example NVDA on Firefox treats <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> similar to a live
        region when using "oninput", but when using "onchange" does not make the announcement when the focus is lost, which it does on Edge and Chrome.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong>Given the myriad combinations of screen reader, operating system, browser, validation display option and event used, I have not provided an expectations section like the tests for other components. My preferred option given
        that the behaviour is the same for all is to use the tabbable region option with the "oninput" event, but you should choose the options that best suit your target audience.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Examples using oninput (immediate validation)</h2>
    
    <section class="section-box">
        <h3>Example one - fake form using the option "Described By With Hint" and the "On Input" event.</h3>

        <EditForm EditContext="@_editContextOne" OnSubmit="HandleSubmitOne">
        
            <BlazorValidated TEntity="InventoryDto" BoxedValidators="_boxedValidators" AddDisplayName="true" />

            <div class="br-input-row">

                <NumericInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" @bind-Value="_inventoryDataOne.UnitsInStock" Required="true" LabelText="Units In Stock" ErrorsLabel="errors" HintText="The number of units currently in stock." UpdateOnInput="true"
                              ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.DescribedByWithHint" ParseErrorMessage="Please enter a valid number for this field type." />

                <NumericInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" @bind-Value="_inventoryDataOne.UnitPrice" Required="true" Format="C" LabelText="Unit Price" ErrorsLabel="errors" HintText="The price per unit." UpdateOnInput="true"
                              ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.DescribedByWithHint" ParseErrorMessage="Please enter a valid number for this field type." />

            </div>

            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;">
                <button class="test-button" type="submit">Submit One to trigger validation on unmodified fields</button>
                <button @ref="ResetButtonOne" class="test-button" type="button" @onclick="ResetEditContextOne">Reset Example One</button>
            </div>
        </EditForm>

    </section>

    <section class="section-box">
        <h3>Example two - fake form using the option "Described By Hint Suppressed" and the "On Input" event.</h3>
        <EditForm EditContext="@_editContextTwo" OnSubmit="HandleSubmitTwo">
        
